Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is "financial point of view" the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 8.2. Evaluation of Acquisition Proposals. <omitted> (c) During the Pre-Closing Period, the Company Board may undertake a Company Recommendation Change <omitted> if, and only if, <omitted> (ii) the Company Board determines in good faith, after consultation with the Company’s outside legal counsel and regulatory compliance advisors, that the failure to make the Company Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement would be inconsistent with the fiduciary duties of the Company Board under applicable Law, (iii) the Company has provided Parent written notice of the Company Board’s intention to make a Company Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement not earlier than 11:59 p.m. New York time on the seventh Business Day after Parent receives such written notice and (iv) if not in connection with an Intervening Event pursuant to Section 8.2(e), the decision to make a Company Recommendation Change is in connection with an Acquisition Proposal or with the Company’s intent to terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement, and the Company shall have complied with clauses (1) through (6), as follows: (1) prior to giving effect to clauses (2) through (6), the Company Board shall have determined that such Acquisition Proposal is a Superior Proposal, (2) the Company shall have made available to Parent orally and in writing the material terms and conditions of such Acquisition Proposal and copies of all written communications (and, if oral, a summary of the material terms of such communications) relating to such Acquisition Proposal in accordance with Section 8.2(b), (3) the Company shall have negotiated in good faith with Parent (and caused its Representatives to negotiate with Parent), to the extent that Parent desires to negotiate, during the seven Business Day period provided in the foregoing clause (iii) of this Section 8.2(c) with respect to such proposed revisions to this Agreement or other proposals made by Parent, if any, so that the Acquisition Proposal would no longer constitute a Superior Proposal, (4) after considering the results of negotiations with Parent and taking into account the proposals made by Parent, if any, after consultation with its outside legal counsel, regulatory compliance advisors, and a financial advisor of nationally recognized reputation, the Company Board shall have determined in good faith that such Acquisition Proposal remains a Superior Proposal, and, after consultation with its outside legal counsel and regulatory compliance advisors, that the failure to make the Company Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement would be inconsistent with the fiduciary duties of the Company Board under applicable Law, (5) if the Company intends to terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement, the Company shall have complied with Section 10.1(d)(i), and (6) the Company Board has considered the ethical standards and corporate social responsibility implications of the Acquisition Proposal. For clarity, the provisions of this Section 8.2(c) shall also apply to any amendment to the financial terms or any other material amendment to any Acquisition Proposal (except that any reference to seven Business Days shall instead be four Business Days) or any successive Acquisition Proposals. (Pages 82-83)\nAnswer:
Choices:

